# Generated by iris. Do not edit; edit the shell's Templates/Iris/kdeglobals.
#
# This is a KDE color scheme (.colors), not kdeglobals itself: the post hook
# Helpers/kde-theme.py merges the Colors:*/WM/ColorEffects:* sections into
# ~/.config/kdeglobals, so the user's non-color keys there survive a re-theme.
# Dolphin and every other KDE app read their palette from kdeglobals through
# KColorScheme and ignore the qt5ct/qt6ct palette entirely, which is why the
# qtct.conf template alone is not enough.
#
# Colors are written as #rrggbb here; the helper converts them to the r,g,b
# triples KConfig reads back as a QColor.
#
# Only bg/surface/dim/fg/accent/red/green/yellow are used. iris swaps the
# meaning of color0/color8/color15 between light and dark wallpapers, and a
# flat hex file has no way to branch on the mode, so those are avoided here.
# bg -> surface -> dim -> fg keeps the same ordering in both modes:
#   views = bg, window/button/tooltip/header = surface, inactive text = dim.

